TRANSITION_STYLE_PRESETS = _presets((
    ("Hard Cut", "Use a clean hard cut at the exact cue with matched screen direction and uninterrupted action continuity."),
    ("Match Cut", "Match shape, composition, color or subject position across the cut so both shots connect as one visual idea."),
    ("Match-on-Action", "Cut during a clearly readable action and continue the same movement, speed and direction in the incoming shot."),
    ("Whip Pan", "End with a fast whip pan and begin the next shot in the same direction, using motion blur to hide the cut."),
    ("Cross Dissolve", "Use a restrained cross dissolve with aligned subject placement and a gradual atmospheric blend between shots."),
    ("Dip to Black", "Briefly dip through black, preserve continuing sound and reveal the next shot from the same narrative beat."),
    ("Dip to White", "Use a short luminous dip to white motivated by a bright source, then resolve smoothly into the next shot."),
    ("Fade Through Color", "Fade through a dominant scene color shared by both shots while preserving rhythm and visual orientation."),
    ("Luma Fade", "Transition according to image luminance, allowing highlights or shadows to reveal the incoming shot progressively."),
    ("Film Burn", "Use a brief organic film-burn flare that consumes the outgoing frame and exposes the incoming image without lingering."),
    ("Light Leak", "A motivated light leak sweeps across the lens, briefly obscures the frame and reveals the next shot beneath it."),
    ("Ink Wipe", "A graphic ink shape spreads across the outgoing image and retracts to reveal the next shot with tactile edges."),
    ("Paper Tear", "A physical paper-tear edge opens across the frame and exposes the next scene as a layered surface beneath it."),
    ("Page Turn", "The outgoing frame bends and turns like a page while the incoming shot remains spatially stable underneath."),
    ("Lens Flare Wipe", "A bright lens flare travels across frame and masks a seamless cut at peak intensity."),
    ("Object Wipe", "A foreground object fully crosses the lens and hides a cut to a matched object or movement in the next shot."),
    ("Foreground Occlusion", "Cut while the camera passes behind a wall, person or prop, maintaining identical camera direction after the occlusion."),
    ("Doorway Passage", "Move through a doorway or portal that naturally replaces the outgoing environment with the incoming scene."),
    ("Speed Ramp", "Accelerate the final movement into the cut and decelerate the matched incoming movement to normal speed."),
    ("Crash Zoom", "Use a rapid controlled zoom to a matching detail, then emerge from that detail in the incoming shot."),
    ("Spin Transition", "Rotate the camera around a stable center and hide the cut in directional rotational blur without disorienting geography."),
    ("Zoom Through", "Push through a clearly defined object or surface and continue the same forward camera path in the next environment."),
    ("Morph Match", "Morph only one matched subject or shape across the transition while keeping scale, position and lighting coherent."),
    ("Graphic Shape Wipe", "Use a clean designed geometric shape to cover the frame and reveal the next shot with exact timing."),
    ("Split-Screen Merge", "Introduce both shots in split screen, align their shared subject or horizon and merge into the incoming full frame."),
    ("Glitch", "Use a very brief controlled digital glitch at the cut; preserve subject identity and avoid persistent image corruption."),
    ("Pixel Dissolve", "Break the outgoing image into restrained pixels that reorganize into the incoming shot while maintaining silhouette readability."),
    ("Smoke Wipe", "A motivated layer of smoke crosses the lens and reveals the incoming scene through changing density."),
    ("Dust Burst", "A short physical dust burst masks the cut and settles naturally into the incoming environment."),
    ("Water Ripple", "A single water-ripple distortion expands across the image and resolves into the next shot without warping subjects afterward."),
    ("Rack-Focus Cut", "Rack focus onto a foreground or background detail and cut at maximum blur to a matched sharp detail in the next shot."),
    ("J-Cut / L-Cut", "Let the incoming sound begin before the visual cut or let outgoing sound continue after it, preserving natural audio continuity."),
))


